  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1408.02 Requirements for Used Oil Processors and Re-refiners",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1408.02 Requirements for Used Oil Processors and Re-refiners.\n\n(a) Used oil processors/re-refiners shall comply with the requirements of Env-Hw 1405, Env-Hw 1408.03 through Env-Hw 1408.11, and, as applicable:\n\n(1) Env-Hw 1406 for generating used oil;\n\n(2) Env-Hw 1407 for transporting used oil and operating a used oil transfer facility;\n\n(3) Env-Hw 1409 for burning used oil for energy recovery, except as provided in (b), below; and\n\n(4) Env-Hw 1410 for acting as a used oil fuel marketer.\n\n(b) A used oil processor/re-refiner that burns used oil for energy recovery shall not be subject to Env-Hw 1409 if:\n\n(1) The used oil is burned in an onsite space heater that meets the requirements of Env-Hw 1406.04; or\n\n(2) The used oil is burned for purposes of processing used oil, which is considered burning incidental to used oil processing.\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
